<title>JAPAN: MITI head says will be able to attend QUAD talks.</title>
<headline>MITI head says will be able to attend QUAD talks.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Minister of International Trade and Industry Shunpei Tsukahara said on Friday that he believes he will be able to leave for Seattle on September 27 to attend quadrilateral trade talks with the United States, Canada and the European Union.</p>
<p>&quot;I think I will be able to leave on the evening of September 27,&quot; Tsukahara said in a news conference.</p>
<p>He also said in the same news conference that Japan's parliament is likely to be dissolved on September 27.</p>
<p>&quot;It is very probable that the parliament will be dissolved (at the beginning of the session),&quot; Tsukahara said.</p>
</text>
